protected boolean hasAdjacentKeywordInEvaluationPath(String keyword) {
    JsonSchema schema = getEvaluationParentSchema();
    while (schema != null) {
        for (JsonValidator validator : schema.getValidators()) {
            if (keyword.equals(validator.getKeyword())) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        Object element = schema.getEvaluationPath().getElement(-1);
        if ("properties".equals(element) || "items".equals(element)) {
            // If there is a change in instance location then return false
            return false;
        }
        schema = schema.getEvaluationParentSchema();
    } 
    return false;
}

Potential NPEs:

- getEvaluationParentSchema() could return null (handled). But schema.getValidators() could be null => NullPointerException when iterating. If schema.getValidators() returns null, for-each will NPE. So need test where getValidators returns null.

- validator.getKeyword() could be null, but keyword.equals(null) is fine (returns false). However if validator is null (i.e., collection contains null), then validator.getKeyword() NPE.

- schema.getEvaluationPath() could be null => NPE when calling getElement. Or getEvaluationPath().getElement(-1) could throw IndexOutOfBoundsException if path empty? getElement(-1) maybe defined to get last element; but if path empty may cause exception. So test for empty evaluation path causing exception.

- getElement(-1) could return null; then "properties".equals(null) returns false (no NPE). So fine.

- schema.getEvaluationParentSchema() could throw something? Not typical.

